      "id": "lights-async",
      "title": "Luminous robots, ASYNC, non-rigid, chirality",
      "assumptions": {
        "visibility": "unlimited",
        "opacity": "transparent",
        "faults": "none",
        "memory": "lights",
        "frames": "chirality",
        "body": "point"
      },
      "summary": "With lights and common chirality, the formable pattern sequences are characterised under ASYNC and non-rigid moves; the number of colours grows with the sequence and is not known to be optimal.",
      "lower_bounds": [
        {
          "measure": "colours",
          "bound": "\\max\\{\\alpha(S)/\\min_i\\alpha(S_i),\\ \\mu(S)^{1/\\alpha(S)}\\}",
          "ref": "Das2020Luminous",
          "bottleneck": "memory",
          "preconditions": [
            "Theorem 18",
            "holds even in FSYNC with rigid moves"
          ]
        },
        {
          "measure": "time",
          "bound": "\\text{impossible}",
          "ref": "Das2020Luminous",
          "bottleneck": "symmetry breaking",
          "preconditions": [
            "Theorem 2: sequences that violate the paper's symmetry conditions"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ref": "Das2020Luminous",
          "role": "best",
          "time": "\\text{finite}",
          "colours": "\\alpha(S)+\\mu(S)+O(1)",
          "assumes": [
            "weak chromatic multiplicity detection"
          ],
          "note": "Introductory and current best: a universal protocol for every formable sequence (Theorem 17). The number of colours is \"bounded but not by a constant\"."
        }
      ],
